{"id": "EUVD-2023-60524", "enisaUuid": "a2ce3f73-cf15-3e0c-9528-69b1a63c4cdd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncifs: fix potential race when tree connecting ipc\n\nProtect access of TCP_Server_Info::hostname when building the ipc tree\nname as it might get freed in cifsd thread and thus causing an\nuse-after-free bug in __tree_connect_dfs_target().  Also, while at it,\nupdate status of IPC tcon on success and then avoid any extra tree\nconnects.", "datePublished": "2025-12-30T12:23:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T21:41:43", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/536ec71ba060a02fabe8e22cecb82fe7b3a8708b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/553476df55a111e6a66ad9155256aec0ec1b7ad0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee20d7c6100752eaf2409d783f4f1449c29ea33d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2023-54280", "GHSA-2c5w-8p3h-w8f6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.52, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a5e6d7a-031a-3225-a713-1be5ee446084", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.2.15"}, {"id": "1d2f1134-1b1e-30a3-a8df-e8cf5319c598", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.4"}, {"id": "52f1eb83-affa-3f3c-9b90-0a55677399e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c88f7dcd6d6429197fc2fd87b54a894ffcd48e8e <536ec71ba060a02fabe8e22cecb82fe7b3a8708b"}, {"id": "6c8a0f3b-965d-3f2f-b4d7-ac2614c03dae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "afe6b742-ac1b-36b6-b934-94b563794ed4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.16"}, {"id": "bdc896d2-c184-3a24-bea7-d0f9150456bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c88f7dcd6d6429197fc2fd87b54a894ffcd48e8e <553476df55a111e6